{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778941350,"nonce":"kEoQbtW/+myE29Yji5Zdz54fBVk=","title":"Ledger git-bug adapter: import/export, labels, cursors, conflicts","message":"## Parent\nUmbrella: 097d2b7 — Mandible canonical issue/work ledger with git-bug import/export.\n\nDepends on: ff6a2bc — Ledger core.\n\n## Scope\nImplement git-bug as an adapter around the canonical ledger, not as the hot-path issue backend.\n\nThis issue owns:\n- idempotent import from git-bug issues into canonical ledger records;\n- export of core issue data from ledger to git-bug;\n- adapter cursor/version/hash tracking for external issue/comment/label state;\n- namespaced label conventions for durable data that fits git-bug well;\n- preservation of existing compatibility labels such as `parent:\u003cid\u003e`;\n- first-class conflict records when external git-bug state diverges from Mandible state;\n- retryable sync jobs with visible status and no normal-path lock dependency;\n- fixture and temp-repo tests where practical.\n\n## Git-bug round-trip target\nThe git-bug mirror should be lossless for core issue fields:\n- title/body;\n- open/closed status;\n- labels;\n- comments;\n- authors/timestamps where available;\n- aliases/provenance where git-bug exposes them;\n- basic issue relationships represented by labels or structured comments.\n\nMandible-specific operational state is metadata-assisted/best-effort unless it has a natural durable git-bug representation.\n\n## Namespaced labels\nUse namespaced labels where they are human-readable and stable, for example:\n- `mandible:kind:umbrella`;\n- `mandible:priority:high`;\n- `mandible:parent:\u003cid\u003e`;\n- `mandible:blocked-by:\u003cid\u003e`;\n- `mandible:related:\u003cid\u003e`.\n\nAvoid exporting volatile live state as labels.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Switching issue routes/CLI to ledger.\n- Mandible-native git-ref transport.\n- Central service sync.\n- Full GitHub Issues adapter.\n\n## Verification\n- Import fixture tests preserving body/comments/status/labels/parent labels/auth-resolved comments.\n- Idempotency tests: repeated imports do not duplicate issues/comments/labels/relationships.\n- Export tests proving dirty/outbox records are mirrored and external IDs/cursors are stored.\n- Conflict tests with simulated remote divergence.\n- Lock contention test or fake adapter test proving failed git-bug access marks sync retryable and does not block ledger reads/writes.\n\n## Done means\nMandible can import existing git-bug corpora into the ledger, export ledger core issue changes back to git-bug, detect external divergence, and report sync state without making normal issue operations depend on git-bug locks.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}